  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two wave generators, placed at position P and position Q, produce water waves with a wavelength of<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0 cm\"></span>. Each generator, operating alone, will produce a wave oscillating with an amplitude of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.0 cm\"></span> at position R. PR is<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"42 cm\"></span> and RQ is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60 cm\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Both wave generators now operate together in phase. What is the amplitude of the resulting wave at R?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"9 cm\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6 cm\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3 cm\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\">zero</li></ol>"
  },
